  "id": "greeting-behavior",
  "term": "greeting behavior",
  "definition": "Greeting behavior is a form of social affiliative behavior shown when a dog responds to a person, such as when first meeting an unfamiliar person or after other social interactions. In this source, its expression varies with the situation and with characteristics of the individual dog.",
